From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:45:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock Mac Chrome speech synthesis with native bindings

Expose Window-only SpeechSynthesis, SpeechSynthesisVoice,
SpeechSynthesisUtterance, SpeechSynthesisEvent and SpeechSynthesisErrorEvent
through the native bridge. Add a stable per-Window synthesis controller,
asynchronous initial voice loading and voiceschanged, native readonly voice
metadata and WebIDL-like construction, conversions and range clamping.

Use a fixed English-US macOS 26.3.1 persona inventory: 23 Apple compact/local
voices and 19 Google remote voices, with Samantha as the default. This is a
synthetic representative inventory, not a measured exhaustive macOS install
or a query of host OS voices. It does not change the reduced UA or Client
Hint platform-version policy in earlier patches, or any Neo hardware values.

Simulate FIFO utterance start/end/error and pause/resume/cancel using the
existing scheduler, with sticky trusted-input activation, native event
instances, insertion-ordered attribute handlers, and cancellation elapsed
time. Duration is synthetic (30 ms per UTF-16 code unit divided by rate,
clamped to 20-2000 ms); no word-boundary or mark precision is fabricated.

Keep queued utterances and event-referenced utterances alive, allow unused
utterances and callback cycles to be collected, and detach queues on frame
teardown and iframe disconnection. Handle scheduler allocation failures
without dangling/double-released persistent handles. Reuse existing event,
identity/finalizer, scheduler and private-property infrastructure.

Scope: silent API mock only. No PCM, audio playback, speech engine, OS voice
installation, network TTS, recognition, or decoding functionality. Google
voices are metadata, not calls to Google. The deterministic inventory,
synthetic duration and incomplete platform-engine behavior remain observable.
Do not change benchmark assertions or enable iframe/worker loading defaults.

References:
https://webaudio.github.io/web-speech-api/#tts-section
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/speech_synthesis.idl
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/speech_synthesis_utterance.idl
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/speech_synthesis_event.idl
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/speech_synthesis_error_event.idl

Validation before export: existing upstream tests 1658/1658; temporary CDP
API diagnostics 107/107 and four navigation teardown cases. Diagnostics
cover shape, native functions, conversions, activation, loading, FIFO,
reentrant cancellation and end-handler pausing, pause/resume, cancellation
timing, event identity, GC survival and reclamation (including callback
cycles), iframe disconnection, worker absence and navigation teardown.
One reviewer pass completed and findings addressed. No new unit tests.
Allocation-failure cleanup was inspected, not fault-injected.
